mma":"pār","gloss":"look"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"k","gloss":"increment"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"k","gloss":"future marker"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"looking for"},{"surface":"காலை","parts":[{"text":"காலை","lemma":"kālai","gloss":"time"}],"gloss":"time"},{"surface":"அன்றே","parts":[{"text":"அன்று","lemma":"aṉṟu","gloss":"it is not"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"is it not?"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஈதல்","parts":[{"text":"ஈ","lemma":"ī","gloss":"give"},{"text":"தல்","lemma":"tal","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"giving"},{"surface":"ஆனான்","parts":[{"text":"ஆனு","lemma":"āṉu","gloss":"cease"},{"text":"ஆன்","lemma":"āṉ","gloss":"third person singular masculine negative suffix"}],"gloss":"he does not cease"},{"surface":"வேந்தே","parts":[{"text":"வேந்து","lemma":"vēntu","gloss":"king"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"vocative/emphasis"}],"gloss":"O King!"},{"surface":"வேந்தற்கு","parts":[{"text":"வேந்தன்","lemma":"vēntaṉ","gloss":"king"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"ku","gloss":"dative case suffix"}],"gloss":"to the king"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சாதல்","parts":[{"text":"சா","lemma":"cā","gloss":"die"},{"text":"தல்","lemma":"tal","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"dying"},{"surface":"அஞ்சாய்","parts":[{"text":"அஞ்சு","lemma":"añcu","gloss":"fear"},{"text":"ஆய்","lemma":"āy","gloss":"second person singular negative suffix"}],"gloss":"you do not fear"},{"surface":"நீயே","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"nī","gloss":"you"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"you indeed"},{"surface":"ஆயிடை","parts":[{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ā","gloss":"that"},{"text":"இடை","lemma":"iṭai","gloss":"place/time"}],"gloss":"meanwhile"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இருநிலம்","parts":[{"text":"இரு","lemma":"iru","gloss":"great/vast"},{"text":"நிலம்","lemma":"nilam","gloss":"earth"}],"gloss":"the vast earth"},{"surface":"மிளிர்ந்திசின்","parts":[{"text":"மிளிர்ந்து","lemma":"miḷir","gloss":"having turned upside down"},{"text":"இசின்","lemma":"iciṉ","gloss":"subjunctive particle"}],"gloss":"if it collapses"},{"surface":"ஆஅங்கு","parts":[{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ā","gloss":"lengthened particle"},{"text":"அங்கு","lemma":"aṅku","gloss":"there/like that"}],"gloss":"like that"},{"surface":"ஒருநாள்","parts":[{"text":"ஒரு","lemma":"oru","gloss":"one"},{"text":"நாள்","lemma":"nāḷ","gloss":"day"}],"gloss":"one day"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அருஞ்","parts":[{"text":"அரு","lemma":"aru","gloss":"rare/difficult"},{"text":"ஞ்","lemma":"ñ","gloss":"nasal increment"}],"gloss":"rare/difficult"},{"surface":"சமம்","parts":[{"text":"சமம்","lemma":"camam","gloss":"battle/war"}],"gloss":"battle"},{"surface":"வருகுவது","parts":[{"text":"வரு","lemma":"varu","gloss":"come"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"ku","gloss":"increment"},{"text":"வது","lemma":"vatu","gloss":"pronominal suffix"}],"gloss":"that which comes"},{"surface":"ஆயின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"āyiṉ","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வருந்தலும்","parts":[{"text":"வருந்தல்","lemma":"varuntal","gloss":"suffering"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"suffering also"},{"surface":"உண்டு","parts":[{"text":"உண்டு","lemma":"uṇṭu","gloss":"there is"}],"gloss":"there is"},{"surface":"என்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"eṉ","gloss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"},{"surface":"பைதலம்","parts":[{"text":"பைதல்","lemma":"paital","gloss":"poor/suffering"},{"text":"அம்","lemma":"am","gloss":"adjectival suffix"}],"gloss":"poor"},{"surface":"கடும்பே","parts":[{"text":"கடும்பு","lemma":"kaṭumpu","gloss":"family/kinsfolk"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"family"}]}],"literal":"Shoulders being pressed, many callouses having formed, / with sparse hair, my many young relatives, / feet aching, having climbed a long distance, / with vine-like waists, the female dancers, / desiring to live, / I will not lie, I will speak the truth: / O descendant of strong men of unretreating determination! / O lord of the unploughed Nāñcil hill with high peaks! / Approaching you for gifts with an undying mind, / this is not the time to look for a ripe opportunity. / The King does not cease giving; to that King, / you do not fear dying. Meanwhile, / if the vast earth collapses, like that, one day, / if a rare battle comes, / my poor family will also suffer.","translation":"With shoulders calloused and pressed by carrying loads, my young relatives with sparse hair, and my female dancers with vine-like waists whose feet ache from climbing long distances, all desire to live. I will not lie; I speak only the truth. O descendant of strong heroes of unretreating determination! O lord of the unploughed Nāñcil hill with high peaks! Approaching you for gifts with an undying hope, this is not the time to wait for a ripe opportunity. You are a king who never ceases giving, and you do not fear death for your sovereign. If the vast earth should collapse, and a fierce battle comes one day, my poor family will surely suffer.","modern":"சுமைகளைச் சுமந்து தோள்கள் அழுந்தித் தழும்புகள் ஏறிய, சிலவாகிய கூந்தலையும் பல சுற்றத்தாரையும் உடைய என் இளைஞர்களும், கால்கள் வருந்த நீண்ட தூரம் மலை ஏறி வந்த கொடி போன்ற இடையை உடைய விறலியர்களும், உயிர் பிழைத்து வாழ விரும்பி உன்னிடம் வந்துள்ளனர். நான் பொய் கூற மாட்டேன், மெய்ம்மையையே கூறுவேன். பின்வாங்காத மன உறுதியும் வலிமையும் உடைய வீரர்களின் வழித்தோன்றலே! உயர்ந்த சிகரங்களை உடைய, உழவு செய்யத் தேவையில்லாத வளமிக்க நாஞ்சில் மலையின் தலைவனே! அழியாத நம்பிக்கையோடு உன்னிடம் பரிசில் பெற வந்த எங்களுக்கு, இது தகுந்த காலமா என்று ஆராய்ந்து பார்க்கும் நேரம் அன்று. நீ இரவலர்க்குக் கொடையளிப்பதை நிறுத்தாத வள்ளல்; உன்னுடைய அரசனுக்காகப் போர்க்களத்தில் சாவதற்கும் அஞ்சாதவன். ஒருவேளை இப்பேரண்டமே தலைகீழாகக் கவிழ்ந்து போவது போல, உனக்கு ஒரு கடுமையான போர் வரும் நாள் உண்டானால், உன்னை நம்பி வாழும் என் ஏழைச் சுற்றத்தாரும் வருந்த நேரிடும்.","explanation":"The poet Marutaṉ Iḷanākaṉār addresses the chieftain Āy Aṇṭiraṉ on behalf of his impoverished troupe of dancers and relatives. He describes the physical toll of their long journey—shoulders calloused from carrying instruments, feet aching from climbing the high, unploughed peaks of Nāñcil hill. The unploughed hill signifies natural abundance, implying that the chieftain has plenty to give. The poet praises the chieftain's generosity and valor but urges him to give gifts immediately without waiting for a 'ripe opportunity' (kālam/patam). He warns that since the chieftain is so brave that he would gladly die in battle for his king, if a war breaks out, the chieftain might perish, leaving the poet's family to suffer in poverty. Therefore, the time to give is now.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}